From 493da4155db1357386ab046a6ada125ccd4c189e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:33:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui_gateway): a refused submit never clears a live turn's
 marker or state [daveey]

Example gateway incident, chat 20260103_000000_abc125: an auto-continue turn started;
shortly afterward a second automatic submit on the same chat was refused
at _admit_prompt_turn (SESSION_NOT_OWNED). The refusal's terminal error frame ran
with the default retire_marker=True, so _retire_turn_marker -> clear_turn_marker
deleted the LIVE turn's marker by session_key (the refused submit never wrote
one). The live turn sat in a clarify; every update-pause hook read "no turn
marker", so nothing withdrew the clarify and hermes-sync refused the core update
over that turn's unpublished admission reservation. In another example the
cross-process variant happened: one process refused a turn and deleted another
process's marker in the shared HERMES_HOME.

- The ownership refusal passes retire_marker=False: a refused submit never
  removes a marker it did not write.
- Backstop: the non-concluding retire path (clear_turn_marker owner_only=True)
  deletes only a marker whose writer_pid is this process or whose writer is dead;
  otherwise it keeps it and logs INFO with the session and writer pid.
- A refusal on a record where an admitted turn is live (_admitted_live_turn, set
  at admission and popped by settle) leaves running, the admission ref, the
  in-flight turn and the client frame alone. _run_admitted_prompt,
  _notif_submit and the auto-continue kickoff read the refusal verdict
  (refusal_spared_live_turn) and release only what that submit took; the Kanban
  caller still rewinds its refused notice. Without a live turn the refusal
  behaves as before. A fresh admission claim drops a leftover record.
- Diagnosis: reservation files record session, work and thread
  (admission_fence state-details reads them back), and a pause hook that finds no
  marker for a running turn whose _active_turn_marker_key matches logs WARNING
  "live turn lost its marker" once per turn.
- #3828 nit: _dropped's ContainmentRefused branch was unreachable (withhold calls
  subjects uncaught), so it is removed; the test name says "rows naming no known
  task" instead of "unidentifiable".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
